<h1>Assets &amp; streaming</h1>
<p>Asset IDs are stable URIs you reference from scenes and scripts. Import records hashes and dependencies; cooking is keyed by content so rebuilds stay fast and deterministic.</p>

<h2>Import a source</h2>
<pre><code>demi asset import assets/textures/brick.png \
  --id asset://textures/brick</code></pre>
<p>This copies the source into the project and writes a <code>*.asset.json</code> manifest. Supported importers: PNG, JPEG, BMP, TGA, QOI, SVG, GIF, WAV, OGG, MP3, FLAC, glTF/GLB, OBJ, IQM, M3D, MP4/WebM/MOV (media builds), JSON data, plus <code>text</code> (<code>.txt</code>, <code>.yaml</code>, <code>.yml</code>). When two importers could claim a source, pass <code>--importer &lt;id&gt;</code>.</p>
<p>After editing the source file, refresh the manifest:</p>
<pre><code>demi asset reimport assets/textures/brick.asset.json</code></pre>
<p>That recomputes <code>source_hash</code>, dependencies, and generated output. Tools that generate sources under <code>assets/</code> call <code>demi asset register-generated</code>.</p>

<h2>Manifest settings</h2>
<pre><code>{
  "format_version": 1,
  "id": "asset://textures/brick",
  "type": "Texture2D",
  "source": "brick.png",
  "settings": {
    "filter": "nearest",
    "wrap": "clamp",
    "mipmaps": false,
    "platform_overrides": {
      "linux": { "compression": "none" },
      "android": { "compression": "astc" }
    }
  }
}</code></pre>
<ul>
  <li>Texture <code>filter</code>: <code>nearest|bilinear|trilinear</code>. <code>wrap</code>: <code>repeat|clamp|mirror</code>.</li>
  <li>Audio: <code>settings.streaming</code> for music and ambience.</li>
  <li>Fonts: <code>settings.variations</code> (for example <code>{"wght": 700, "opsz": 24}</code>).</li>
  <li>Data: <code>settings.schema</code>, <code>content_type</code>, <code>tags</code> — see <a href="{{ path('docs_page', {slug: 'game-data'}) }}">Game data</a>.</li>
  <li><code>platform_overrides</code> lets one manifest differ per platform without duplicate assets.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Terrain assets</h2>
<p>Terrain sources use <code>*.terrain.json</code>, type <code>Terrain</code> and importer <code>terrain_heightfield</code>. Scenes place them through <code>Terrain3D.asset</code>. Select a placement to sculpt or paint in the scene Viewport; its Terrain Graph contains generation settings and modules. Apply changes to the shared asset without embedding recipes in the scene. The editor and build tools prepare the generated data; shipped games load the cooked payload. See <a href="/docs/terrain">Terrain assets and editing</a> for creation, graph editing and shipping.</p>

<h2>Atlases</h2>
<p><code>TextureAtlas2D</code> packs sprites from a units descriptor: <code>page_width</code>, <code>page_height</code>, <code>padding</code>, <code>bleed</code>, and <code>sprites[]</code> entries with <code>id</code>, <code>source</code>, <code>pivot</code>, <code>border</code>, and <code>animation_tag</code>. <code>FontAtlas2D</code> rasterizes glyphs with <code>pixel_height</code>, <code>page_size</code>, <code>padding</code>, <code>glyph_ranges</code>, and <code>fallbacks</code>.</p>

<h2>Startup preload and addressable groups</h2>
<p>The project <code>assets</code> array is startup preload only — anything else loads on demand or with its scene. Group related assets for batched streaming:</p>
<pre><code>{
  "format_version": 1,
  "id": "asset-group://level_one",
  "roots": ["asset://levels/one", "scene://game/level_one"],
  "budget": {
    "resident_mb": 192,
    "decoded_mb": 384,
    "upload_ms_per_frame": 3
  }
}</code></pre>
<p><code>budget</code> records resident and decoded memory limits and the per-frame upload budget. Measure the loaded group's actual memory use with <code>Assets.memory_report()</code> when tuning these values.</p>

<h2>Loading from Lua</h2>
<pre><code>local Assets = require("demi.assets")
local Audio = require("demi.audio")
local Game = {}

local request, err = Assets.load("asset://music/theme")
if not request or request == 0 then error(err) end
local started = false

function Game:on_update()
    if Assets.is_ready(request) then
        if not started then
            Audio.play("asset://music/theme", { bus = "music", loop = true })
            started = true
        end
    else
        local p = Assets.progress(request)
        -- p.stage names the stage; p.fraction is 0.0 … 1.0
    end
end

function Game:on_stop_music()
    Assets.cancel(request)                  -- only matters while pending
    Assets.unload("asset://music/theme")    -- release this owner
end

return Game</code></pre>
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Call</th><th>Returns</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><code>Assets.load(uri)</code></td><td>Request ID and error string. Keep the ID to poll or cancel this load.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>Assets.is_ready(request)</code></td><td>Boolean, <code>true</code> when the request reached <code>ready</code>.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>Assets.progress(request)</code></td><td>Table with <code>stage</code>, <code>fraction</code> (0…1), asset counts, byte totals, and <code>error</code>. Stages: <code>resolve</code>, <code>read</code>, <code>decode</code>, <code>upload</code>, <code>ready</code>, <code>failed</code>, <code>cancelled</code>.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>Assets.text(uri)</code></td><td>Cached contents of a loaded text asset, or <code>nil</code>, plus an error string.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>Assets.memory_report()</code></td><td>Current pending, decoded, and resident bytes plus per-asset entries.</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
<p>Scene transitions build an implicit group from the <code>scene://</code> root and activate atomically at a frame boundary. A failed reload keeps the previous resident version.</p>
<p>For other loaded resources, <code>Assets.text(asset_id)</code> returns cached text or <code>nil</code> plus an error string; <code>Assets.reload(asset_id)</code> picks up a changed source; <code>Assets.memory_report()</code> reports pending, decoded, and resident bytes and per-asset owners.</p>

<h2>Cooking</h2>
<pre><code>demi cook --platform linux</code></pre>
<p>Output is <code>generated/cooked/&lt;platform&gt;</code> plus <code>cook.manifest.json</code> listing every included path and hash. Cache keys include importer identity and version, normalized settings, source hashes, platform, and package provenance — so a rebuild only redoes what changed.</p>

<h2>Portable asset packs</h2>
<pre><code>demi asset export \
  --output brick_pack.demipack --asset asset://textures/brick

demi asset import-package brick_pack.demipack
 </code></pre>
<p><code>.demipack</code> is a deterministic container: versioned JSON index plus sorted file data with IDs, manifest paths, sizes, and checksums. Import rejects absolute paths, <code>..</code>, checksum failures, and implicit overwrites.</p>

<h2>Collider assets</h2>
<pre><code>demi asset collider assets/models/crate.glb.asset.json \
  --id asset://colliders/crate</code></pre>
<p>Generates a <code>Collider3D</code> asset from a model. Triangle-mesh results are static-only; convex or compound collider assets can support moving bodies. See <a href="{{ path('docs_page', {slug: 'colliders'}) }}">Colliders</a> for authored collider sources and attachment.</p>

<h2>Performance budgets</h2>
<pre><code>demi asset budget games/my_game/demi.project.json --platform android</code></pre>
<p>Reports usage against project <code>performance_budgets</code>: frame time, draw calls, resident assets, visible instances, unique meshes, triangles, texture memory, lights, shadow lights, and transparent draws.</p>
